WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.447 --> 00:00:05.360
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> <b>Fascinating facts about sugar and salt.</b>

2
00:00:06.735 --> 00:00:13.417
At different times in history, both sugar and salt were called ‘white gold’

3
00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:17.062
because they were so expensive and difficult to get.

4
00:00:17.294 --> 00:00:21.850
And there are many more interesting facts about sugar and salt…

5
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:28.728
Salt is used to make glass, washing powder, and paper.

6
00:00:30.657 --> 00:00:37.035
People often think that sugar makes children more active or that it makes them behave badly.

7
00:00:37.357 --> 00:00:41.841
However, there is no strong scientific evidence of this.

8
00:00:43.967 --> 00:00:47.540
Salt was very valuable in ancient Rome.

9
00:00:47.808 --> 00:00:53.204
Soldiers were paid extra money called ‘salarium’ especially to buy it,

10
00:00:53.347 --> 00:00:56.294
and this is where the word ‘salary’ comes from.

11
00:00:58.081 --> 00:01:05.031
Scientists use sugar to make different kinds of plastic, for example, for food packaging.

12
00:01:07.228 --> 00:01:12.927
Only 6% of the salt used in the USA is used in food;

13
00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:19.716
the remaining 94% is used for things like farming and de-icing roads.

14
00:01:21.985 --> 00:01:26.630
Sure and sugar are the only two words in the English language

15
00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:30.185
that begin with ‘s’ and are pronounced ‘sh’.

16
00:01:32.573 --> 00:01:36.911
In the UK, there’s a club for people who collect the little packets of

17
00:01:36.911 --> 00:01:42.442
sugar you get when you order tea or coffee in a café or restaurant.

18
00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:50.749
Salt removes red wine stains (though probably not from your new white carpet).

19
00:01:52.571 --> 00:01:57.627
If you put sugar into a vase of flowers, the flowers last longer.

20
00:01:59.538 --> 00:02:05.363
The body of an average adult has about 250 g of salt.

21
00:02:05.702 --> 00:02:10.687
It helps oxygen to travel around the body and makes muscles work.

22
00:02:12.473 --> 00:02:19.494
Salzburg, the city in Austria where Mozart was born, means ‘castle of salt ’.

23
00:02:21.281 --> 00:02:28.856
Christopher Columbus introduced sugar to the Americas in 1493 on his second voyage.